assertion  XCU.sh-compound.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.1
class      required
says       ( list ) runs the list in a subshell: its assignments and
           directory changes do not remain, and its status is that of the
           list.
test       t/001-subshell-group.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.1
class      required
says       { list; } runs the list in the current environment and its status
           is that of the list.
test       t/002-brace-group.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4/redirection shall apply to all the commands within the compound command
class      required
says       A redirection after a compound command applies to every command
           inside it that does not redirect that descriptor itself.
test       t/003-redirections.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.2
class      required
says       for sets the variable to each word of the expanded list in turn
           and runs the body each time; the variable keeps the last value;
           the list is expanded (parameters, field splitting, pathname,
           arithmetic, substitution).
test       t/004-for-items.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.2
class      required
says       A for with no items does not run its body and has status zero;
           otherwise its status is that of the last body run. Without in,
           the list is "$@".
test       t/005-for-empty-and-status.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.3
class      required
says       case runs the compound list of the first clause whose pattern
           matches (patterns separated by | are alternatives, a leading ( is
           allowed), and only that one.
test       t/006-case-select.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.007
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.3
class      required
says       The status of case is zero when no pattern matches (whatever the
           status before it), and otherwise the status of the clause that
           ran.
test       t/007-case-status.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.008
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.3
class      required
says       The case word and the patterns are expanded (tilde, parameter,
           command and arithmetic substitution, quote removal); an expanded
           pattern keeps its special characters unless quoted; no pattern
           after the first match is expanded.
test       t/008-case-expansions.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.009
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.3
class      required
since      2024
says       A clause ended by ;& also runs the list of the next clause
           without testing its pattern, and so on until a clause ended by ;;
           (or the last one).
test       t/009-case-fallthrough.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.010
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.4
class      required
says       if runs the then list when its condition succeeds, else tries
           each elif, else runs the else list.
test       t/010-if-select.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.011
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.4
class      required
says       The status of if is that of the then or else list that ran, or
           zero when none ran; the status of a condition is $? at the start
           of the next list.
test       t/011-if-status.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.012
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.5
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.6
class      required
says       while runs its body as long as the condition succeeds, until as
           long as it fails.
test       t/012-while-until.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-compound.013
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.5
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.4.6
class      required
says       The status of while and until is that of the last body run, or
           zero if the body never ran; $? in the body is the status of the
           condition.
test       t/013-loop-status.sh
